# 5. UI/UX & Accessibility Notes

Following the codx-junior design system (DaisyUI + dark theme):

- **Button semantics:** "Compare" is a **supporting action** → `btn-info btn-outline`, hover `btn-active` shows active state. It sits inline with the other toolbar buttons, wrapped in the existing `overflow-x-auto snap-x` container (mobile-safe).
- **States covered:** default, hover (DaisyUI `btn-outline`), active (`btn-active`), and it only renders when `hasReference && finished && !editMode` (no dead button).
- **Feedback:** the info banner (`alert alert-info alert-sm`) makes the diff baseline explicit — never rely on color alone.
- **Accessibility:**
  - Add `aria-label` to the button if you want the icon-only (mobile) form to be screen-reader friendly:
    ```vue
    :aria-label="`Compare with previous version${referenceLabel ? ` (${referenceLabel})` : ''}`"
    ```
  - The "Compare" label is already shown on `sm+`; the `title` covers tooltip/mouse users.
  - `DiffViewer` handles keyboard/scroll natively via `@git-diff-view`.
- **Anti-patterns avoided:**
  - ❌ Not overloading the existing "View diff" icon (that is the *file* diff) — a **separate** control keeps mental models clean.
  - ❌ Not silently changing the diff baseline — the banner + button state make it visible.
  - ❌ No new colors introduced — uses existing `info` semantic + info channel text (`text-info`).

